# process-rule-pins scans the skill tree and the roles in place: the pinned step and rule-body files, adversary.md and remediator.md,
# the flat skill files, steps/, rule-bodies/ and the roles for the retired-range count and the lead-address arm (never
# extensions/, overrides/ or templates/), and layer-contract.yaml for the consumer-owned exclusions. The root is found by
# the dist-layout marker pair core/skills/ai-dlc + core/team-roles. The advisor gate hook is read for its
# ADVISOR_GATE_WINDOW default, which section 4g binds to the count SKILL.md Rule 32 touchpoint I states.
!core/skills/ai-dlc/
core/team-roles/
!core/hooks/ai-dlc-advisor-gate.sh
# The --mark arm runs the engine against a scratch file.
!core/scripts/wait-for-deliverable.sh
core/fixtures/lib/mutant.sh
# Section 4i reads partition-review-diff.sh as text: its THRESHOLD header, its AI_DLC_ key and its built-in default.
core/scripts/partition-review-diff.sh
